1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:07,000
All of the events that happened after Fushi went into his deep slumber in Renril.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Bon told to Fushi.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Please don't die and leave me behind.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Everyone was so very kind.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Right to the end.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
To Takunaha?

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,000
What brought this on? How'd you manage to get it?

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,000
Fushi said goodbye as Gugu left for Takunaha.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
How did you come to?

10
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Love a sleep life.

11
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:34,000
F Hari!

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:57,000
In Namely Tanaka.

13
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:26,980
Thank you.

14
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:56,980
Thank you.

15
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:11,780
Excellent. Go get them.

16
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:14,520
Welcome to all of our new first graders.

17
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,020
Congratulations on your very first day at Minamoto Elementary School.

18
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:21,200
Hello there.

19
00:02:22,620 --> 00:02:25,460
Nice to meet you. I'm March. Why don't we be friends?

20
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:28,360
Your name is March? March is a weird name.

21
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:31,760
It's nice to meet you too. I'm March. Why don't we all be friends?

22
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:34,280
What's that thing you have on the top of your head?

23
00:02:34,500 --> 00:02:36,820
Let me see. Isn't it cute?

24
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:38,760
My mommy made it for me.

25
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:43,020
Don't you know that you're really not supposed to bring anything like this into school?

26
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:44,900
It's not allowed. My mommy told me.

27
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:47,440
Well, why not? You have something in your hair as well.

28
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:50,360
Mine are allowed, but yours is just a silly decoration.

29
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:52,520
That's not fair! You have decorations!

30
00:02:52,520 --> 00:02:55,640
I've always had these ribbons in my hair, so they don't really count.

31
00:02:55,740 --> 00:02:58,640
Well, I've always had this on my head as well, so damn!

32
00:02:58,660 --> 00:02:59,660
Oh, yeah? How long?

33
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:01,440
For 500 years!

34
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:04,940
500 years!

35
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:06,060
Liar!

36
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:13,140
I'm not lying, teacher! One of the new students in the school is a crazy fat liar!

37
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:21,660
I really hope March is doing okay. She'll be fine. She's very sociable, and Bond's there too.

38
00:03:22,060 --> 00:03:24,720
Hey, Aiko, you'll need the first year's entrance. It's over there.

39
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:26,020
Thanks. See you later.

40
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:27,860
Go knock him out!

41
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:28,540
Oh, yeah!

42
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:30,580
Hey, everyone.

43
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,920
President! Good morning to you!

44
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:39,100
Oh, hey, Fushi. You're close to Mizuha, right?

45
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:43,420
It's just that we've been looking for her name, but we can't find her on any of the class lists.

46
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:44,100
Huh?

47
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:48,680
She transferred to another school. Something to do with her father's work, I think.

48
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:50,880
How come we didn't hear anything about this before?

49
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:53,240
Well, it was pretty sudden.

50
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:56,060
Hana, you really didn't know about this?

51
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,640
I had no idea. Sorry.

52
00:03:58,140 --> 00:04:02,640
Right. You don't wear your hair accessory anymore, so I thought something might have happened.

53
00:04:06,060 --> 00:04:11,920
How'd it go?

54
00:04:12,340 --> 00:04:15,660
Looks like they're not in. Do you think they've already moved out of town?

55
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:17,580
I think they're just ignoring us.

56
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:18,780
Why do you think that?

57
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:23,640
I've been checking in on Mizuha's place for a while. I've never seen them moving out.

58
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:25,420
Oh, good. That means...

59
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:28,400
It's Mizuha's birthday tomorrow, isn't it?

60
00:04:29,080 --> 00:04:32,080
I want to see her smile again, even if it's just one more time!

61
00:04:32,280 --> 00:04:34,360
I would do anything to make that happen! Anything!

62
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,840
Me too. I wonder what it would take to make her smile again.

63
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:41,340
Right. Now smile!

64
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:41,440
Smile!

65
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:50,760
Hello there, Marge. Did you have fun?

66
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:56,480
Oh, dear. What's the matter? Is it something that happened at school today?

67
00:05:00,900 --> 00:05:02,260
Oh, hi, Bun.

68
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:07,860
Why, hello, Mimory. Look, Marge. It's Mimory. Did you know she goes to your school, too?

69
00:05:08,160 --> 00:05:13,920
Oh, Marge. Right. She's the one who Fushi was talking about. His mom?

70
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:16,060
Huh? What did you say?

71
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:18,220
Nothing. Is she okay?

72
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:22,780
Well, I think she's feeling pretty fed up with school right now.

73
00:05:23,940 --> 00:05:25,980
That's just like me. It's true.

74
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:32,400
Oh, Fushi.

75
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:34,120
What's Marge doing over there?

76
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:38,780
Oh, she's just making mud balls with Mimory. Is something the matter, Fushi?

77
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:42,540
Gugu sent me a message. He wants to see Marge dressed up for school.

78
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:45,620
Good timing. She was crying until just now.

79
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:46,680
She was?

80
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:50,760
I'm afraid she doesn't like school, but now she's finally smiling.

81
00:05:51,220 --> 00:05:52,420
Great, but how come?

82
00:05:52,420 --> 00:05:53,840
Well, just watch.

83
00:05:55,980 --> 00:06:00,020
Oh, right. The attention grabbed no jutsu.

84
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:02,860
Something that remained after Mimory left.

85
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:06,160
Something that makes a connection between people.

86
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:08,940
Something that makes a connection across time.

87
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:10,940
Something that brings smiles.

88
00:06:11,020 --> 00:06:13,320
It's Mizuha's birthday tomorrow, isn't it?

89
00:06:14,620 --> 00:06:14,760
Oh.

90
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:21,060
Maybe I should send her a gift.

91
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:25,940
Happy birthday to me.

92
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:31,980
Happy birthday to me.

93
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:37,240
Happy birthday, dear Mimory.

94
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:37,820
Mizuha.

95
00:06:37,820 --> 00:06:43,860
Izumi's PC is supposed to have some sort of records of Mizuha in there somewhere.

96
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:46,740
We can print the photos out and give them to her as a gift.

97
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:48,380
That's a really nice idea, Fushi.

98
00:06:48,740 --> 00:06:51,660
The password is 0406.

99
00:06:53,200 --> 00:06:53,700
There.

100
00:06:54,700 --> 00:06:57,720
At the very least, I want her to know the truth.

101
00:06:57,980 --> 00:07:02,760
That all her mother wanted was to remember her exactly the way she was.

102
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:04,840
She didn't want to forget all those memories.

103
00:07:05,420 --> 00:07:06,260
I bet.

104
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:10,100
Okay, it's all done.

105
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,580
They're all taped inside the book.

106
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:17,200
What are you all doing?

107
00:07:17,540 --> 00:07:18,360
Check it out.

108
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:20,540
We made a really cool birthday gift for Mizuha.

109
00:07:20,620 --> 00:07:21,800
A special photo album.

110
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:24,900
I want to make it even cuter.

111
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:29,480
I got a bunch of new stickers yesterday.

112
00:07:29,940 --> 00:07:31,380
Wow, looks great.

113
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:34,720
There.

114
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:40,260
Huh?

115
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,040
How come you were in that shed?

116
00:07:42,220 --> 00:07:43,520
What were you doing in there, Fushi?

117
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:44,000
Nothing.

118
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:56,200
Why do you guys look so gloomy?

119
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:57,160
Is something wrong?

120
00:07:57,420 --> 00:08:00,120
We were just updating them about what happened up until now.

121
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:04,820
So we were just discussing whether we should do something about Mizuha disappearing.

122
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:07,260
But unfortunately, we don't know what we can do.

123
00:08:08,120 --> 00:08:10,760
I don't think you need to worry too much about it, Hana.

124
00:08:11,280 --> 00:08:13,440
Something happened between you and Mizuha, though.

125
00:08:13,440 --> 00:08:14,200
Is that right?

126
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:21,920
I think it's more important to know what she's doing than where she is right now.

127
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:24,060
So, does that mean you do know?

128
00:08:24,260 --> 00:08:25,840
You know what Mizuha's up to, Fushi?

129
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:26,900
No.

130
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:32,520
If only there was a way that we could get her to see that she has people around her who really do care about her.

131
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:36,800
Although, I'm not entirely sure what we would say to her even if we did see her.

132
00:08:36,920 --> 00:08:40,080
And if we said the wrong thing to her, then we might lose her forever.

133
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:42,820
Well, in that case, let's keep it simple.

134
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:45,340
And the best way is to ask this question.

135
00:08:45,560 --> 00:08:47,600
Hana, do you want to see Mizuha again?

136
00:08:48,160 --> 00:08:49,860
Yeah, I really do.

137
00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:51,200
I miss her.

138
00:08:51,200 --> 00:09:00,100
There's a chance that she might not let us in, but let's at least try and drop by her place anyway.

139
00:09:00,320 --> 00:09:03,580
Yeah, good idea. I made her this new birthday gift as well.

140
00:09:03,580 --> 00:09:09,860
Was it you who dropped this in our mailbox?

141
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:12,200
You must be your dad!

142
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:14,220
It's a special birthday gift for Mizuha!

143
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:16,920
Well, I'm sorry, but I'm sure she'll refuse it.

144
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:19,000
My daughter has already moved on.

145
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,240
She's cut off her past.

146
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,800
We do not intend to return.

147
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:25,480
But where are you guys moving to?

148
00:09:25,480 --> 00:09:27,260
Somewhere you can never come or visit.

149
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:29,800
I'm leaving with my daughter first thing tomorrow.

150
00:09:30,240 --> 00:09:33,040
And we're going so far that you won't be able to be friends anymore.

151
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:35,400
I hope that you all understand.

152
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:43,940
Well, it looks like there's no point in going.

153
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:47,480
That was nice of him to go out of his way to bring it back to us.

154
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:47,940
It was.

155
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:50,300
No, this fell out.

156
00:09:51,080 --> 00:09:52,800
I thought we taped everything in.

157
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:53,320
Huh?

158
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:55,620
I don't remember this photo.

159
00:09:56,720 --> 00:09:58,220
My beloved family.

160
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,100
What is this?

161
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:03,380
We should still go check out Mizuha's new place.

162
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:05,140
I think we should give up on that.

163
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:06,900
We'd just be causing more trouble for her.

164
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:08,120
Crap!

165
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:11,260
I still haven't confessed to Mizuha how I feel!

166
00:10:11,480 --> 00:10:12,520
I have to do it!

167
00:10:12,920 --> 00:10:14,100
So I'm coming with!

168
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:15,900
It's my last chance!

169
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:19,900
Well then, you have to tell her how you feel, Yuki!

170
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,520
I know, right?

171
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:22,980
Let's do it, Vice President!

172
00:10:23,380 --> 00:10:24,720
We all stand behind you.

173
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:26,260
Let's go!

174
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:26,820
Yeah!

175
00:10:30,820 --> 00:10:34,520
Our guest today is the Renro weed removal expert, Harumaki,

176
00:10:34,520 --> 00:10:36,080
of the Tasty Peach Foundation.

177
00:10:36,540 --> 00:10:36,840
Hello!

178
00:10:37,500 --> 00:10:39,100
Bond's on the TV again.

179
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:40,820
This one's live broadcast.

180
00:10:41,020 --> 00:10:42,520
He's famous now!

181
00:10:42,860 --> 00:10:45,720
Would you mind telling Bond to stop skipping his work at school?

182
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:49,140
He hasn't been there in ages, and the principal is really furious with him.

183
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:51,180
See you later!

184
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:54,480
Hey, Tanari, wait up!

185
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:54,960
Huh?

186
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:56,580
Could you do me a favor?

187
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:58,960
I left my school body in the custodian's room.

188
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:01,000
Do you mind checking to see if it's still hidden?

189
00:11:01,300 --> 00:11:02,120
But why me?

190
00:11:02,540 --> 00:11:03,900
I'm skipping school today.

191
00:11:03,940 --> 00:11:06,280
I'm telling Mizuha how I feel about her today!

192
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:08,040
It's my very last chance!

193
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:09,520
And I'm going to help him.

194
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:10,020
Huh?

195
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:11,300
You get it?

196
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:12,860
It's an important day.

197
00:11:12,860 --> 00:11:15,820
Let's go!

198
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:17,520
But I don't get it!

199
00:11:40,100 --> 00:11:41,060
Welcome back, Fushi!

200
00:11:41,060 --> 00:11:42,000
How'd it go?

201
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:44,320
They live near her grandfather's house now.

202
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:45,700
Underground, probably.

203
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:49,240
I think it's connected to that place where Fenn and Nixon went.

204
00:11:49,800 --> 00:11:52,200
All right, so we're stepping into the enemy stronghold!

205
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:54,340
The Occult Research Club!

206
00:11:54,760 --> 00:11:55,440
Let's go!

207
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:56,500
ORC, fight!

208
00:11:56,760 --> 00:11:58,420
ORC, fight!

209
00:11:58,560 --> 00:12:00,620
It's not the ORC or the Handicrafts Club.

210
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:02,440
This isn't even a club event.

211
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,220
Hold on!

212
00:12:03,340 --> 00:12:04,140
You're all coming?

213
00:12:04,260 --> 00:12:06,120
That was the agreement, after all.

214
00:12:06,120 --> 00:12:07,300
Of course we're all coming!

215
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:10,080
Vice Principal Yuki's romantic life is on the line!

216
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:12,260
You're coming with us as well, aren't you, Hana?

217
00:12:12,680 --> 00:12:13,540
Uh, yeah.

218
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:16,280
Well, this will be my first time skipping school.

219
00:12:16,760 --> 00:12:17,700
All right, then.

220
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:21,160
But the second it gets dangerous, we're turning back, okay?

221
00:12:21,720 --> 00:12:22,420
Roger that!

222
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:22,740
Sir!

223
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:25,000
Hey, I'm the leader of the Occult Research Club!

224
00:12:25,060 --> 00:12:26,200
It's pretty far, isn't it?

225
00:12:26,220 --> 00:12:27,180
Guess we'll take the bus.

226
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:28,280
Come on, guys!

227
00:12:28,360 --> 00:12:29,360
I said I'm the leader!

228
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:35,560
Oh, and by the way, when you take the detergent back, do you mind taking this gas canister as well?

229
00:12:36,060 --> 00:12:39,900
What a giant pain in the butt.

230
00:12:39,900 --> 00:12:49,600
You didn't hide your body well at all!

231
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:51,360
Oh, man.

232
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:53,280
You still need me to help you.

233
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:57,220
Huh?

234
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:04,540
Hey, I used to use this bow.

235
00:13:04,960 --> 00:13:05,900
Man, what a throwback!

236
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:08,300
Wait, why do you have these weapons here?

237
00:13:13,460 --> 00:13:16,280
Come to think of it, what are you up to anyway, Fushi?

238
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:18,140
We're here.

239
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:23,160
Maybe we should go and say hello to her grandpa?

240
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,180
We shouldn't say hi to the enemy.

241
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:26,840
Wait, he's an enemy?

242
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:27,340
Enemy?

243
00:13:27,780 --> 00:13:29,060
I like the sound of that!

244
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:29,680
Her grandpa?

245
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:31,040
I don't understand.

246
00:13:31,900 --> 00:13:32,380
Ugh!

247
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:34,540
Do we really need to enter through here?

248
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:36,560
The tunnel's closed tight with a steel door.

249
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:39,200
I could break it open, but that would take too long.

250
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:47,900
It's the entrance to a city of mazes!

251
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,220
Mizuha's really beyond these tunnels?

252
00:13:51,880 --> 00:13:52,780
That's unreal.

253
00:13:53,780 --> 00:13:55,980
Looks like it's time for the brains of this unit.

254
00:13:56,160 --> 00:13:57,660
Send us Suzuhiko to shine!

255
00:13:57,660 --> 00:13:59,440
I'll use the map on my laptop.

256
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:02,140
There's no internet down here!

257
00:14:02,160 --> 00:14:02,620
That way.

258
00:14:03,100 --> 00:14:04,080
The one on the right.

259
00:14:06,680 --> 00:14:08,780
Be careful and try not to slip.

260
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:10,740
How did you know it's this one?

261
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:14,280
Fushi has this cool way of connecting to the roots through the tunnels.

262
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:16,560
So that means you can sense which is the right way.

263
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:19,940
